From fa27a28e48384d280b73cf0b00a7199b80e24605 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mojyack <mojyack@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 01:03:23 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Add -Zoffload-emit and -Zoffload-codegen flags to enable
 distributed compilation

This implements the necessary compiler flags to split the compilation
pipeline into three distinct phases for distributed compilation:
- `-Zoffload-emit`: Halts compilation after frontend evaluation and
  serializes all CGUs (including the allocator module) and rlink metadata.
- `-Zoffload-codegen`: Restores codegen state from the serialized rlink
  metadata and CGUs to independently execute the LLVM codegen phase.
- `-Zlink-only`: Native host linkage phase using the resulting object
  files.
